-- title:
--   H BConsistency Error Add Mdq Add Dnoteq Le Over All Outcomes Error
-- statement:
--   **The bad-line consistency term and both algebraic losses fit inside the total error.** Assume $0<d$, $d\le q$, and $d+1\le k$, and let $\varepsilon,\delta,\gamma,\zeta$ be nonnegative errors. Write $H$ for the bad-line consistency error and $E$ for the over-all-outcomes error. Then
--
--   $$
--   H+\frac{md}{q}+\frac{k^2}{q}\le E.
--   $$
--
--   The numerators are coerced into the error type. This is the arithmetic aggregation used after the bad-line and tuple-averaging estimates.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
